{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00603",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.99,
      "end_seconds": 15.98,
      "duration_seconds": 14.99,
      "text": "Mrs Whitcombe, good morning. I've got the letter here from your pharmacist, saying your pulse felt uneven when she checked it. Who've you brought with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 18.94,
      "end_seconds": 34.55,
      "duration_seconds": 15.61,
      "text": "This is Maria, she looks after me in the week. She's marvellous, she does the most wonderful soup, leek and potato, though I tell her not so much pepper."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 35.88,
      "end_seconds": 48.23,
      "duration_seconds": 12.35,
      "text": "Hello, doctor. I'm her carer, I live in at the moment. Mrs Whitcombe asked me to come in and help her remember things."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 49.66,
      "end_seconds": 61.37,
      "duration_seconds": 11.71,
      "text": "That's a good idea. Now, Mrs Whitcombe, what did you notice that made you go to the pharmacy in the first place?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 62.22,
      "end_seconds": 77.07,
      "duration_seconds": 14.85,
      "text": "Well, I was in for something else, really, I wanted a new hairbrush, the old one lost half its bristles, and she said would I like my pulse done."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 77.93,
      "end_seconds": 88.5,
      "duration_seconds": 10.57,
      "text": "Ah, so the pharmacist did it on her own initiative. And since then, have you felt anything yourself?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 89.9,
      "end_seconds": 101.31,
      "duration_seconds": 11.41,
      "text": "A fluttering, here in my chest, like a bird caught in a net. Comes and goes, been about two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 102.77,
      "end_seconds": 110.47,
      "duration_seconds": 7.7,
      "text": "A fluttering, on and off, for about two weeks. Anything else with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 111.67,
      "end_seconds": 120.52,
      "duration_seconds": 8.85,
      "text": "I get a bit light-headed if I stand up too fast, but I put that down to age."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 121.3,
      "end_seconds": 132.53,
      "duration_seconds": 11.23,
      "text": "She did go wobbly on Tuesday in the kitchen, doctor. She held on to the counter and it passed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 134.63,
      "end_seconds": 147.62,
      "duration_seconds": 12.99,
      "text": "Thank you, Maria, that's helpful. Mrs Whitcombe, I need to ask you something that may seem to come out of nowhere. Do you have any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 149.78,
      "end_seconds": 158.35,
      "duration_seconds": 8.57,
      "text": "Allergies? Oh dear. I think I might be allergic to something, but I couldn't tell you what."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.62,
      "end_seconds": 165.27,
      "duration_seconds": 4.65,
      "text": "Go on, what makes you think so?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 167.84,
      "end_seconds": 187.49,
      "duration_seconds": 19.65,
      "text": "Years ago, something gave me a reaction. I can't remember the thing, or what it did. Perhaps it was a cream, or perhaps a tablet. Or the wallpaper paste, in the old house."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 189.54,
      "end_seconds": 198.21,
      "duration_seconds": 8.67,
      "text": "She's said that to me as well, doctor. A bad turn after something, but never a name."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 199.93,
      "end_seconds": 216.31,
      "duration_seconds": 16.38,
      "text": "So a possible allergy, no name, nothing known about what it did. We'll note it as uncertain and be careful. Maria, can you help us find out from her old records?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 218.19,
      "end_seconds": 222.6,
      "duration_seconds": 4.41,
      "text": "I'll ask her daughter. She keeps the folders."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 223.35,
      "end_seconds": 228.88,
      "duration_seconds": 5.53,
      "text": "Yes, Helen has everything in folders. Labelled, even. Colour coded."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 249.57,
      "end_seconds": 255.6,
      "duration_seconds": 6.03,
      "text": "Lovely. Now, let me do your observations. Arm out for me, please."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 256.54,
      "end_seconds": 266.97,
      "duration_seconds": 10.43,
      "text": "Blood pressure is 142/88. Pulse is 92, and it's irregular. Temperature is 36.6 °C, and oxygen saturation is 97%."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 269.12,
      "end_seconds": 274.69,
      "duration_seconds": 5.57,
      "text": "Is that good? I never know which number matters."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 275.78,
      "end_seconds": 289.79,
      "duration_seconds": 14.01,
      "text": "Mostly fine. The irregular pulse is what I'd like to look at more closely. I'd like to do an ECG today, which is a tracing of the heart's rhythm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 291.1,
      "end_seconds": 297.67,
      "duration_seconds": 6.57,
      "text": "Will it hurt? Is it the one with the sticky pads?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 299.47,
      "end_seconds": 307.59,
      "duration_seconds": 8.12,
      "text": "Sticky pads, yes, ten of them, but no pain. The nurse will do it before you leave."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 309.58,
      "end_seconds": 314.0,
      "duration_seconds": 4.42,
      "text": "I'll hold your handbag, Mrs Whitcombe."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 316.7,
      "end_seconds": 323.32,
      "duration_seconds": 6.62,
      "text": "Thank you, dear. Doctor, can I still have my evening sherry?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 324.66,
      "end_seconds": 334.68,
      "duration_seconds": 10.02,
      "text": "A small one is not a problem today. Tell me, how much do you drink, as a rule?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 337.63,
      "end_seconds": 346.97,
      "duration_seconds": 9.34,
      "text": "Oh, I like a drink of an evening, just a small sherry. The odd glass at Christmas, otherwise."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 347.86,
      "end_seconds": 354.45,
      "duration_seconds": 6.59,
      "text": "That's modest. Let's see what the tracing shows before I say more."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 355.75,
      "end_seconds": 363.7,
      "duration_seconds": 7.95,
      "text": "Of course. I don't want to make a fuss, I know you're busy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 364.81,
      "end_seconds": 377.0,
      "duration_seconds": 12.19,
      "text": "Not at all. If the fluttering gets worse, or you feel faint or have chest pain, please ring us straight away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 378.51,
      "end_seconds": 387.15,
      "duration_seconds": 8.64,
      "text": "I'll keep an eye on her and make a note of when it happens."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 389.98,
      "end_seconds": 396.87,
      "duration_seconds": 6.89,
      "text": "Maria writes everything in a little book. She's got me down as 'chatty'."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 398.84,
      "end_seconds": 408.01,
      "duration_seconds": 9.17,
      "text": "Accurate, I'd say. If the fluttering gets any worse, please ring us, and if you faint, call an ambulance."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 409.92,
      "end_seconds": 412.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "Right. Thank you, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 415.18,
      "end_seconds": 423.01,
      "duration_seconds": 7.83,
      "text": "Mind how you go, both of you. The ECG room is on your left."
    }
  ]
}
